[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Matshio7/gk2-vanilla-plus/main/docs/nexus/header.png[/img]

[size=5][b]Ultrawide, more frames and smart quality-of-life tools – without changing the game.[/b][/size]

[size=3]No gameplay changes · No game files touched · Your saves stay vanilla[/size]

[youtube]YOUTUBE-ID[/youtube][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]Why you'll want it[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Your whole monitor, finally.[/b] 21:9 and 32:9 unlocked – and rain and snow reach the edges too.
[*][b]More FPS from the same PC.[/b] The game hides half its graphics switches. Vanilla+ puts them in one menu – on the author's PC the built-in benchmark went from [b]58 to 89 FPS[/b] on Medium.
[*][b]Less tabbing out.[/b] Pin recipes and quests, see what's on each weekday, back up and restore saves – all in game.
[/list]
[center][size=3][b]Free · One-click installer · English, Deutsch, Français, Español, Русский, 中文[/b][/size][/center]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Matshio7/gk2-vanilla-plus/main/docs/nexus/section-01-ultrawide.png[/img][/center]
[list]
[*]Unlocks the resolutions the game hides: [b]2560×1080, 3440×1440, 3840×1080, 5120×1440[/b] and more.
[*][b]Rain and snow fill the full width[/b] on ultrawide screens and zoomed-out views – same density, toggle in the mod menu.
[*]The main menu fills the sides with a soft blurred copy instead of black bars.
[/list]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Matshio7/gk2-vanilla-plus/main/docs/nexus/section-02-performance.png[/img][/center]
[list]
[*][b]Hidden graphics settings[/b] in the mod menu ([b]F9[/b]): soft PC or cheaper console shadows, ambient occlusion (HBAO), point lights, back light, water, clouds, render mode.
[*][b]Frame rate cap or VSync[/b] with a target FPS – a locked 60 on laptops, handhelds and Macs.
[*][b]Graphics benchmark[/b]: one click tests every tier plus your own settings, gives a score and a recommendation. Nothing is changed.
[*][b]FPS overlay[/b] ([b]F10[/b]): FPS, 1% low, frame time, CPU, GPU, RAM, VRAM, resolution, clock, in-game day and time – any corner.
[*][b]OLED black[/b]: pure black around the map instead of dark grey.
[/list]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Matshio7/gk2-vanilla-plus/main/docs/nexus/section-03-quality-of-life.png[/img][/center]
[list]
[*][b]Pin recipes[/b], blueprints and town buildings – a have / need list at the screen edge that turns green when you're ready. Controller: press both sticks.
[*][b]Pin quests[/b] and single crafts like blockages – pins are kept per save.
[*][b]Week plan[/b] ([b]F6[/b]) and a daily reminder – what's possible on which weekday. Spoiler-free: only what you've unlocked.
[*][b]Saves[/b]: save overview in the main menu, "Save now", extra autosave, [b]backups with one-click restore[/b].
[*][b]Camera[/b]: zoom presets ([b]F5[/b]), separate indoor zoom, smooth mouse-wheel zoom.
[*][b]Screenshots[/b] ([b]F12[/b]) at up to 4× resolution, [b]hide HUD[/b] ([b]F7[/b]).
[*]Readability: size of the mod displays, high contrast. Pause in background, skip intro logos.
[*]Mod menu in the game's own look – [b]F9[/b] or the [b]Mods[/b] button in the main and pause menu.
[/list]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Matshio7/gk2-vanilla-plus/main/docs/nexus/section-04-install.png[/img][/center]
[b]Windows[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download the main file and extract it.
[*]Double-click [b]Installieren.bat[/b] (SmartScreen: "More info" → "Run anyway").
[*]Click [b]Install[/b] – the game folder is found for you. Start the game and press [b]F9[/b].
[/list]
The installer also sets up BepInEx 5.4.23.5, the standard Unity mod loader.

[b]Mod manager / manual:[/b] the optional file [b]GK2-VanillaPlus-Manual[/b] has the game-folder layout – extract it into the folder with GraveyardKeeper2.exe.

[b]Steam Deck / Linux (Proton):[/b] copy [i]installer/files[/i] into the game folder and add the launch option [code]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="winhttp=n,b" %command%[/code]
[b]macOS (CrossOver):[/b] copy [i]installer/files[/i] into the game folder, then Wine configuration → Libraries → [i]winhttp[/i] = native, builtin.
Under Wine the mod menu also offers a [b]controller fix[/b] against stutter with PlayStation controllers.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Matshio7/gk2-vanilla-plus/main/docs/nexus/section-05-updates.png[/img][/center]
Click [b]Track[/b] at the top of this page to get notified about new versions. To update, download the new main file, run [b]Installieren.bat[/b] → [b]Update[/b]. Your settings are kept, and a "What's new" window shows what changed.
[i]This Nexus edition never connects to the internet.[/i]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Matshio7/gk2-vanilla-plus/main/docs/nexus/section-06-safe-by-design.png[/img][/center]
[list]
[*][b]No gameplay changes[/b] – balance, progress and content stay exactly as Lazy Bear made them.
[*][b]No game files touched[/b] – everything loads through BepInEx.
[*][b]Saves stay vanilla[/b] – uninstall any time ([b]Installieren.bat[/b] → [b]Uninstall[/b], optionally with BepInEx) and your saves still load in the unmodded game.
[*][b]Source on GitHub[/b] – read every line: [url=https://github.com/Matshio7/gk2-vanilla-plus]github.com/Matshio7/gk2-vanilla-plus[/url]
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]FAQ[/b][/size]
[b]Does it work with my existing save?[/b] Yes. Load it as usual – nothing in the save changes.
[b]Do I need an ultrawide monitor?[/b] No. Performance and quality-of-life features work on every screen.
[b]Something's wrong?[/b] Post in the [b]Posts[/b] tab and attach [i]<game folder>\BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/i].

[center][size=4][b]Enjoying it? An [color=#93d36c]Endorse[/color] helps other keepers find it.[/b][/size][/center]

[size=2]Mod packs: you may include GK2 Vanilla+ [b]unmodified[/b] in free mod packs, with credit ("GK2 Vanilla+ by McFly7") and the license file. Modifying it, re-uploading it as your own or removing credits is not allowed. [url=https://github.com/Matshio7/gk2-vanilla-plus/blob/main/LICENSE.md]License[/url]
Pinning inspired by "Recipe Pin" by farfars (own implementation). Fan project, not affiliated with Lazy Bear Games or tinyBuild.[/size]

[line]

[spoiler=Deutsch]
[size=4][b]GK2 Vanilla+ – die PC-Version, die Graveyard Keeper 2 verdient[/b][/size]
Ultrawide, mehr FPS und clevere Komfort-Werkzeuge – ohne das Spiel zu verändern. Kein anderes Gameplay, keine Spieldateien angefasst, Spielstände bleiben kompatibel.

[b]Ultrawide[/b]
[list]
[*]Schaltet 2560×1080, 3440×1440, 3840×1080, 5120×1440 und mehr frei.
[*]Regen und Schnee füllen die ganze Breite – auch beim Rauszoomen. Im Mod-Menü abschaltbar.
[*]Das Hauptmenü füllt die Seiten mit einer weichen, unscharfen Kopie statt schwarzer Balken.
[/list]
[b]Leistung[/b]
[list]
[*]Versteckte Grafik-Schalter im Mod-Menü ([b]F9[/b]): Schatten (PC oder sparsame Konsolen-Schatten), HBAO, Punktlichter, Gegenlicht, Wasser, Wolken, Render-Modus.
[*]Bildraten-Limit oder VSync mit Ziel-FPS – stabile 60 auf Laptops, Handhelds und Macs.
[*]Grafik-Benchmark mit Score und Empfehlung (beim Autor: Mittel 58 → 89 FPS mit Vanilla+-Einstellungen).
[*]FPS-Anzeige ([b]F10[/b]) mit 1%-Low, Frametime, CPU, GPU, RAM, VRAM, Wochentag und Uhrzeit im Spiel. OLED-Schwarz.
[/list]
[b]Komfort[/b]
[list]
[*]Rezepte, Baupläne, Stadtgebäude, Quests und Einzel-Handwerk anpinnen – Haben/Brauchen am Bildschirmrand, pro Spielstand gespeichert. Controller: beide Sticks drücken.
[*]Wochenplan ([b]F6[/b]) und spoilerfreie Tagesübersicht.
[*]Spielstand-Übersicht, „Jetzt speichern“, zusätzlicher Autosave, Backups mit Wiederherstellen.
[*]Kamera: Zoom-Stufen ([b]F5[/b]), Innenraum-Zoom, Mausrad-Zoom. Screenshots ([b]F12[/b]) bis 4×, HUD ausblenden ([b]F7[/b]).
[*]Lesbarkeit, hoher Kontrast, 6 Sprachen. Mod-Menü über [b]F9[/b] oder den Button [b]Mods[/b].
[/list]
[b]Installation (Windows):[/b] Hauptdatei laden und entpacken → [b]Installieren.bat[/b] doppelklicken (SmartScreen: „Weitere Informationen“ → „Trotzdem ausführen“) → [b]Installieren[/b]. Spiel starten, [b]F9[/b] drücken.
[b]Mod-Manager / manuell:[/b] optionale Datei [b]GK2-VanillaPlus-Manual[/b] in den Ordner mit GraveyardKeeper2.exe entpacken.
[b]Steam Deck / Linux:[/b] [i]installer/files[/i] in den Spielordner kopieren, Startoption [code]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="winhttp=n,b" %command%[/code]
[b]macOS (CrossOver):[/b] [i]installer/files[/i] kopieren, Wine-Konfiguration → Bibliotheken → [i]winhttp[/i] = nativ, builtin.
[b]Aktualisieren:[/b] oben auf [b]Track[/b] klicken, um über neue Versionen informiert zu werden. Neue Hauptdatei laden, [b]Installieren.bat[/b] → [b]Aktualisieren[/b]. Einstellungen bleiben erhalten. Diese Nexus-Ausgabe verbindet sich nie mit dem Internet.
[b]Deinstallieren:[/b] [b]Installieren.bat[/b] → [b]Deinstallieren[/b] – danach ist das Spiel wieder genau wie vorher.
Weitergabe in kostenlosen Modpacks [b]unverändert[/b] und mit Namensnennung erlaubt, Verändern nicht.
[/spoiler]
